sandra let's bring in chad wolf former  acting dhs secretary under president  trump chad welcome  so what's the practical impact of this  supreme court ruling to the men and  women on the front lines at our southern  border so look this is a disappointing  ruling and why is it disappointing  because the program worked and not only  do border patrol agents and other law  enforcement support the program i think  most americans support the program as  well we used it in 2019 and 2020 and we  saw results it helps not only secure  that border but it absolutely helps  control  the asylum process and it gets those  that need asylum protections quicker  access to those protections instead what  you have today is a catch and release  system that allows these individuals  into the country for years at a time so  i think the practical effect is that the  cartels the smugglers and the  traffickers are going to use this court  decision a decision that was you know  pushed by the biden administration to  again attract and lure more individuals  to come to the united states and what  they'll sell them on is to say there is  now zero chance that you're going to be  put into mpp or the remaining mexico  program there's going to be almost 100  chance that you're going to get released  into the united states we have brand new  reaction from texas governor greg abbott  let's put it on the screen quote the  supreme court's decision upholding dhs's  termination of the remain in mexico  policy will only embolden the bide  administration's open border policies  reinstating and fully enforcing remain  in mexico would deter thousands more  migrants from making that deadly trek  and president biden should take that  simple step to secure the border because  because it is the only humane thing to  do  it's obviously been a heartbreaking week  in the state of texas with migrants and  in a very difficult at least year and a  half yeah absolutely i think it's  important to remember look the court's  decision doesn't tell dhs that they must  remove or eliminate the program it's  still up to the bind administration they  still have the choice to implement this  program or not to improve it to make it  better but at the end of the day look  they're making a number of decisions i  think most americans are throwing their  hands up and saying why are you doing  this why are you allowing the situation  at the border to remain out of control  and every month we see the illegal  apprehension numbers get worse and worse  and worse and so the question is if you  don't want mpp  what else do you want in its place what  other program or procedures are you  going to put in place to control the  situation on the border and i've said  this before the cartels want one thing  and that's predictability to run their  businesses and the bite administration  is giving them that one thing the  predictability from day one which is  they're not putting any new measures in  place to deter the illegal behavior  instead they throw their hands up and  they say well this is just how it is and  most americans are just going to have to  accept this and that's just the wrong  strategy it's the wrong approach you're  not putting america first you're putting  them last when you do that do you think  the supreme court in effect is saying to  the white house and congress like sit  down and come up with a plan  well i think so again they didn't rule  on the merits of mpp in fact as you read  the opinion and the majority says  dhs actually has legal authority to do  this congress gave them the authority to  do this uh the question is whether they  could they could rescind the program or  not and so they obviously have that  authority now uh but look you can you  can look at congress needing to to make  some changes but the executive branch  and we proved this out in 2019 and 2020  has a lot of authority they just have to  have leadership and will to use that to  make some hard decisions  along that border to control the border  and to deter this illegal behavior and  we just haven't seen any of that  leadership any of that vision laid out  over the past 15 or 16 months instead  it's just open borders and you continue  to see these astronomically high  apprehension numbers that we've never  seen before you had one month back in  march of 2000 when it got over 200 000  illegal apprehensions one month in the  byte administration we have five months  so it just tells you sort of where we're  going and where the trend line is going  nearly out of time but what's the morale  of men and women at our border on the  front line well it's terrible um you  know if you're border patrol agents  you've been you've been asking your  leadership to reinstate remain a mexico  program and so you see the news here  which is the supreme court ruling but  you know that your political leadership  has been against this program from day  one so slowly and surely they've removed  every tool in your tool belt to address  the border crisis the last thing that  you have left is title 42 and they hear  that their political leadership wants to  remove title 42 and that's in the courts  as well and so  you don't have a lot of confidence on  where this is going and there's no light  at the end of the tunnel and that's hard  for these folks who live and breathe uh  who live in these border communities  every day chad wolfe thanks so much for  your time thank you your analysis hi  everyone i'm brian kilmeade i want you  to do me a favor i want you to click to  subscribe to the fox news youtube page  this is the only way that i know for  sure that you're not going to miss any  great commentary any great news bites  any great interviews coming your way on  fox you can get it all here on youtube  so subscribe right now
 

